    <!--
      Payment Plans is NOT exposed in the V2 tree.

      `realestate.payment.plan` is declared with `_name` by two modules that do
      not inherit each other. `real_estate_developer`'s class wins the registry
      (52 live fields); `atmta_real_estate`'s four fields — start_after,
      start_after_unit, unit, interval — survive only as orphaned
      ir_model_fields rows and SQL columns. Both modules also ship a list and a
      form view at the same priority, and Odoo resolves BOTH actions to
      `atmta_real_estate`'s, which reference the fields that no longer exist.

      Result, verified in the browser on this database:
          Developer   > Pricing      > Payment Plans  -> Odoo Client Error
          Real Estate > Configuration> Payment Plans  -> Odoo Client Error
          "realestate.payment.plan"."start_after" field is undefined.

      This is a live defect that predates Wave 0 and is broken from every menu
      in the system today. Wave 0 does not fix legacy and will not ship a
      destination it knows is broken. Restore this menu in the wave that
      resolves the ownership question in 17_RISKS_AND_OPEN_DECISIONS.md §1.
    -->
    <menuitem id="menu_price_history" name="Price History" parent="menu_pricing" sequence="40"
              action="real_estate_developer.action_price_history"/>
    <menuitem id="menu_price_bulk" name="Bulk Price Update" parent="menu_pricing" sequence="50"
              action="real_estate_developer.action_price_bulk_update"/>

